{"name":"August Moon","hex":"#e6e1d6","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"august","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Awe-inspiring, majestic, noble, venerable.","Of noble birth."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make ripe; ripen.","To bring to realization."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/august"},{"term":"moon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Moon (“the Earth's only permanent natural satellite”)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any natural satellite of a planet.","The light received from the Moon; moonlight."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moon"}],"entries":[{"title":"August Moon","blocks":[{"text":"August Moon was an American R&B singer known as Mr. Wiggles, a songwriter, producer, record label owner, and community activist."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/db/August_Moon_%28Mr._Wiggles%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/August_Moon","wikidata":"Q124260396"},{"title":"August","blocks":[{"text":"August is the eighth month of the year in the Julian and Gregorian calendars. Its length is 31 days."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Reeve_and_Serfs.jpg/330px-Reeve_and_Serfs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/August","wikidata":"Q122"},{"title":"Moon","blocks":[{"text":"The Moon is the only natural satellite of Earth. It orbits Earth in an elliptical path, at a distance that varies over the year, averaging around 378,000 kilometers (235,000 mi). It completes an orbit in relation to Earth and the Sun (synodically) every 29.5 days. The Moon and Earth are bound by gravitational attraction, which is stronger on the sides facing each other. The resulting tidal forces are the main driver of Earth's tides, and have pulled the Moon t